course: dictionary
lesson: 9908
title: Tally: counting and matching
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tally is a way of keeping count. You draw a small line for each thing you count, and every fifth line is drawn across the four before it, making a gate. «Keeping a simple tally shows the real numbers.» A tally is a record of a count.
explain: Tally can also be a verb. To tally up means to count or add up. Tally can also mean the total so far: a goal tally is how many goals a player has scored this season.
explain: When two things tally, they match. «Tallymen are party helpers who watch the Irish count and keep their own tally to guess the result early.» Their own count has to agree with the real count for their guess to be useful. If two numbers tally, they agree.
fact: A tally is a record of a count, often made with small lines.
fact: A tally chart is a quick way to record data: draw four lines, then a fifth line across them to make a gate of five.
fact: «Tally» can mean the total counted so far, as in a goal tally.
fact: «Tally» as a verb means to count or add up, and «tallied» is the past tense.
fact: If two things tally, they match or agree.
exercise: «Keeping a simple tally shows the real numbers.» What is a tally? | A player who scores goals | A loud party game with music | A sweet, sticky bread | *A record of a count, often made with small lines
exercise: A striker's goal tally this season is 12. What does goal tally mean? | *The total goals counted so far | The goals she wants to score next season | A rule about kicking the ball | The name of her team
exercise: Mia checks that her money tallies with the receipt. What does tallies mean here? | They are both lost | They are both very large | They are both wrong | *They match and agree
test: How do you make a gate of five on a tally chart? | *Draw four lines, then one line across them | Draw five lines in a row | Draw a circle round four dots | Write the number five in the middle
test: Jamal says «The two stories tally.» What does he mean? | They are very long | *They agree and match | They are both about dogs | They are both funny
exam: «Tallymen keep their own tally to guess the result early.» Why do tallymen keep their own tally? | To collect sweets from the guests | To hide from the other helpers | To make the party louder | *To count and guess the result before the official count
